%description:

Tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks:linux-quickack -- the quickack mode acknowledges the first data of a connection at once.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with delayedAcksEnabled, the delayed ACK of Linux: a quickack budget
(ACKs at once at the start of a connection, after out-of-order data and after a long
pause) [...]".

The classes: rfc (false), and three facets of true (LinuxTcp); this is the facet of the
quickack mode at the start. The code: the first data segment gives the quickack budget, and
an ACK goes at once while the budget lasts (TcpAlgorithmBase::dataArrivedAtoUpdate(),
receiveSeqChanged()). This test separates the facet from "rfc": with false, the lone
segment waits for the delayed ACK timer.

Host under test: host2, the receiver. Peer: host1 sends one segment of 100 bytes, the first
data of the connection. Observation: level 1, the ACK of host2 within 1 ms of the arrival.

%# parameter: Tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks
%# class: linux-quickack
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxQuickack")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the segment of 100 bytes at host2")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .describe("the ACK of host2, at once")
                  .within(0.001));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxQuickack compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.adaptiveDelayedAcks = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAdaptiveDelayedAcksLinuxQuickack: PASS
